From e609d42f26014b385e8d3490bac29e7b63bf5eb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 07:18:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 2 (cont.): UpDownBase/DomainUpDown and
 AutoCompleteStringCollection

- UpDownBase : ContainerControl (faithful base), re-parents NumericUpDown onto it.
  Adds InterceptArrowKeys/ReadOnly/TextAlign/UpDownAlign/PreferredHeight and the
  abstract UpButton()/DownButton(); NumericUpDown implements them by stepping Value
  by Increment with Minimum/Maximum clamping, and gains ReadOnly/Text overrides.
  Re-parenting through ContainerControl/ScrollableControl is safe: the spin button
  is not IScrollableBoxBase, so scrollbase is simply null and every scroll path
  no-ops.
- DomainUpDown : UpDownBase + DomainUpDownItemCollection. Full item/selection model
  (Items/SelectedIndex/SelectedItem/Wrap/Sorted, UpButton/DownButton cycling,
  SelectedItemChanged). Backed by a read-only GTK entry showing the selected item;
  GTK has no composite text+spin widget, so the arrow glyphs are not rendered
  (documented visual deviation) while the programmatic API is complete.
- AutoCompleteStringCollection : IList with the typed string members and the
  CollectionChanged event, values/shape from the net48 reference assembly.

Net48 public types present 568->571 (missing 466->463). Full suite green at 2302
(+8 functional tests: NumericUpDown value stepping/clamping, DomainUpDown
selection/wrap/sort, AutoCompleteStringCollection semantics).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
